    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c654fbc4_ca990d3a",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 4936,
      "author": {
        "id": 1343198
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-19T12:24:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Framework transport type is defined from TRANSPORT_CELLULAR(0).\nResolver network type is defined from 1(NT_CELLULAR) and NT_UNKNOWN is 0.\nThey should be having the same mapping becuase they are the same meaning. Therefore I redefine transport types in IDnsResolver.aidl.\n    const int TRANSPORT_UNKNOWN \u003d 0;\n    const int TRANSPORT_CELLULA \u003d 1;\n    const int TRANSPORT_WIFI \u003d 2;\n    const int TRANSPORT_BLUETOOTH \u003d 3;\n    const int TRANSPORT_ETHERNET \u003d 4;\n    const int TRANSPORT_VPN \u003d 5;\n    const int TRANSPORT_WIFI_AWARE \u003d 6;\n    const int TRANSPORT_LOWPAN \u003d 7;\n\nBefore TRANSPORT_* is sent to resolver, I should remap TRANSPORT_*. \nThis can make framwork and resolver has the same tranport type mapping.\nAnd the default value is reasonable becuase it\u0027s TRANSPORT_UNKNOWN that is defined in     \nResolverParamsParcel.aidl.\nIf we don\u0027t remap, the default value would be empty or we should choose a number for it. I think remapping should be better than prevous options.",
      "parentUuid": "15f6b81d_58152190",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4936,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 4936,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "6cabd278c5bc5303d368a27d988a11bcdf642a20",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3114dc87_e5e841c8",
        "filename": "tests/net/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityServiceTest.java",
        "patchSetId": 18
      },
      "lineNbr": 4936,
      "author": {
        "id": 1306837
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T00:59:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC there is no such case that framework will pass TRANSPORT_UNKNOWN to resolver, right? It will be empty array if there is no transport.\n\nIf it is only locally used in resolver, does it resolve the problem if we make unknown -1 locally in resolver?\n\nIt will be efforts to maintain such table, and given that it is totally the same with table in NetworkCapabilites but only 1 number shifted, I\u0027m not sure this is good idea.",
      "parentUuid": "c654fbc4_ca990d3a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4936,
        "startChar": 60,
        "endLine": 4936,
        "endChar": 87
      },
      "revId": "6cabd278c5bc5303d368a27d988a11bcdf642a20",
